    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2053339139693814144",
      "url": "https://x.com/momblogger/status/2053339139693814144",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/momblogger/status/2053339139693814144",
      "text": "This morning, I started my daily 10,000 steps. I have been counting them since 2015.\n\nSome days in Manila traffic. Other days between the rows at our  Agnep Heritage Farm in Benguet. Last week I was testing a new soap recipe for Aninag. There is a column on AI governance sitting on my desk.\n\nIt is Mother’s Day. I am thinking about all of it.\n\nThe girls are grown, but the mothering did not stop. It went into the farm and the soap and the writing and the steps.\n\nFor a long time, I thought “Mother” was the title that held everything. It still holds a lot. It is not the only one.\n\nHappy Mother’s Day to all of us.\n\n#Mothers #MothersDayCelebration #DignityInAging",
